# ClangSharpPInvokeGenerator response file for the DRM format constants.
#
# Separate from pipewire.rsp for one reason: these constants are #define macros
# (DRM_FORMAT_NV12 and friends expand through fourcc_code()), so emitting them needs
# --generate macro-bindings. That switch is fatal on the PipeWire header set, which uses
# CompoundLiteralExpr macros ClangSharp 21 cannot translate - see the note in pipewire.rsp.
# drm_fourcc.h has no such macros, so it generates cleanly on its own.
#
# --file is deliberately absent: generate.sh supplies the single composite root. Naming it
# here as well makes it a second root, and ClangSharp then emits every declaration twice.
#
# These are kernel uapi: the values are ABI and never change. They are the pixel-layout
# (fourcc) and tiling-layout (modifier) halves of a dmabuf description. PipeWire negotiates
# the modifier through SPA_FORMAT_VIDEO_modifier but does not itself declare these values,
# which is why they come from libdrm rather than the PipeWire headers.

--traverse
/usr/include/libdrm/drm_fourcc.h
--include-directory
/usr/include/libdrm

--namespace
PipeWire.NET.Drm
--method-class-name
DrmFourcc

--generate
macro-bindings

--config
file=single
codegen=preview
types=unix

# drm_fourcc.h also declares one static inline helper. This header is traversed for its constants
# only; a translated function body is untested surface that the mapping in DrmFormat does not use.
--exclude
drm_fourcc_canonicalize_nvidia_format_mod
